  "body": "### Summary\nAs a member, I want a request that ends \"cancelled\" without anyone cancelling it to be retried or reported everywhere, as the reader does since #566, so that no screen is left blank or spinning. Today each screen treats `.cancelled` as \"the user went away\", whoever cancelled.\n\n### Scenario\nThe transport answers `.cancelled` while our task was not cancelled (the #566 case: `URLSessionTransport.map` turns any `URLError.cancelled` into `.cancelled`, `Packages/HFRKit/Sources/HFRNetwork/Transport/URLSessionTransport.swift:166-171`).\n- First load of the Messages list: empty list, no message, no \"Réessayer\".\n- First load of a profile: \"Chargement du profil…\" for ever.\n- Alertes Qualitay: \"Chargement…\" for ever on a first load started by \"Réessayer\" or \"Actualiser\".\n- Post filter: the banner vanishes with no result and no message.\n\n### Evidence (`7a61018f`)\n- The reader's rule: `App/SwiftHFR/Reader/TopicReaderModel.swift:547-550` and `:619-621` (retry once, then an error; \"never a screen left waiting\").\n- `App/SwiftHFR/Navigation/ContentLoader.swift:66-67`: `.failure(.cancelled)` clears `isLoading` and sets neither value nor error; `App/SwiftHFR/Profile/UserProfileView.swift` and `App/SwiftHFR/Messages/MessageListView.swift` have no state for \"no value, no error, not loading\".\n- `App/SwiftHFR/FilteredPosts/FilteredPostsModel.swift:229-230`: `if case .network(.cancelled) = error { return .success(nil) }`, then `:125-130` returns on `guard let batch`.\n- `App/SwiftHFR/QualityAlerts/QualityAlertsModel.swift:166-171`: sets `isLoading = false` and returns with `hasLoaded` false; `QualityAlertsView.swift:75` shows `ProgressView` while `!model.hasLoaded`.\n\n### Fix\nOne rule, shared with the reader: `.cancelled` means \"stopped\" only when the run was really cancelled (`Task.isCancelled` or a generation change); otherwise retry once, then show the generic failure. Put it in `ContentLoader.load` and reuse it in the filter and the AQ list.\n\n### Tests (fail before the fix)\n- `ContentLoaderTests.aCancellationNobodyAskedForIsRetriedOnce`: the operation throws `.cancelled` once, then returns a value.\n- `FilteredPostsModelTests.aCancellationNobodyAskedForIsAFailure`; `QualityAlertsModelTests.aCancellationNobodyAskedForEndsTheLoad` (`hasLoaded && failure != nil`).\n\nHow often the transport cancels unasked outside the reader is not measured. Related: #108 (a cancelled request must never complete the next load), #566.\n\nRework model: Sonnet 5.5, reviewed by Opus 5.5.\n\nFound by #775 (cloud/r775-fable, Fable 5.2). Reviewed at `dev-swift` @ `7a61018f`; read from the code, not run on a device unless stated.\n\n---\n_Generated by [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)_",
